CheckProof -- first-order TSTP proof checker (ProoVer entry).

BUILD
  make                 # produces bin/CheckProof  (needs a C11 compiler + libm)
  ./starexec_build     # equivalent, for StarExec

The whole engine is one self-contained translation unit; no external
dependencies beyond the C standard library and libm.  CheckProof is
built from the same sources as the FindProof equational prover (the
CASC UEQ entry); the binary name selects the checking mode.

STAREXEC CONFIGURATION
  bin/starexec_run_default PROOF.p
      Validates every derived step of a first-order TSTP proof and
      writes one SZS verdict (VerifiedGood / VerifiedBad / Unknown).
      Wall-clock limit from $STAREXEC_WALLCLOCK_LIMIT (default 30s).

RUN (manual)
  bin/CheckProof --szs PROOF.p

INPUT   First-order TSTP proofs (fof/cnf records with inference
        annotations), by refutation, closing with $false.  The problem
        file named by the proof's file() directives is loaded from the
        adjacent Problems/ directory and every input leaf is verified
        against it.  Its include('F') directives are read too: F
        resolves against the problem's directory, $TPTP, then the
        current directory, and include('F', [n1, ...]) contributes only
        the listed formulas.  When an include cannot be read, leaves
        still match only formulas that were read, and a leaf citing a
        formula found nowhere abstains instead of failing.
OUTPUT  One SZS verdict line; when a step is rejected, the faulty step
        is named in a following comment.

VERDICT POLICY (abstain-by-default; ProoVer scores a wrong VerifiedGood
-10 and a wrong VerifiedBad -1):
  VerifiedGood  every record parsed, every leaf verified against the
                problem file, every derived step positively confirmed
                (internal rule check, or the external-ATP hook), names
                unique, citation graph acyclic, $false root confirmed.
  VerifiedBad   only on a DEMONSTRATED violation: a countermodel of a
                thm/cth claim, a leaf semantically differing from the
                problem formula it cites, a reused Skolem symbol, a
                citation cycle, duplicate names with differing formulas.
  Unknown       everything else, including anything undecided within
                the resource bound.

EXTERNAL ATP (permitted by the ProoVer rules for thm/cth steps):
unsettled steps are discharged by re-exec'ing this same binary as a
prover (THVM_CHECKPROOF_PROVE=1) on exactly the step and its premises,
budgeted against the proof wall.  THVM_PROOFCHECK_ATP=path overrides
the oracle binary; =0 disables the hook.
